/// ZlibStream — an opaque `zlib:zstream()` handle.
///
/// Erlang's `zlib:open/0` answers a zstream and every other `zlib` call takes
/// one back. The checker types FFI results with this class so a zstream stays
/// a named type (rather than `Dynamic`) and can only be handed back to `zlib`.
///
/// A ZlibStream has no protocol of its own: its contents are not inspectable,
/// and sending it any message other than the `Object` protocol (identity and
/// equality such as `=:=`) is a type error.
///
/// This is an opaque-handle class in the "Object" kind of the three-kind
/// model (ADR 0067): no `state:`/`field:` slots and not instantiable from
/// Beamtalk. It is declared only so FFI specs have a type to name.
///
/// The class is static only: at run time the value is a Reference, so `x class` answers
/// that and `x isKindOf:` against this class is always false.
/// Process-scoped (ADR 0103): a zlib stream belongs to the process that
/// opened it, so passing one in an actor message or capturing it in a block
/// sent to an actor warns, as it does for a `Port`.
sealed typed Object subclass: ZlibStream
  handleScope: #process
